[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://src/core/document.gd" id="1_doc"]

[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_doc")
id = &"d13_protocol_4"
title = "Protocol 4 — Observation"
byline = "rev. 1966, framed at the observer station"
hand = 0
body = "WORK UNIT 1615-C
STANDING PROCEDURE — OBSERVATION

4.1  The chamber shall be dark except for
     the schedule luminaire.

4.2  The observer stands at the lamp. The
     subject may look toward the lamp at
     any time.

4.3  The observer shall not speak except on
     the schedule. The subject shall not be
     told the schedule.

4.4  A run is not concluded until the
     observer leaves the lamp.

NOTES ON 4.2

The observer's position is not incidental.
A subject deprived of exterior cues will
attend to the only varying feature of the
environment, and will attend to it whether
or not they are told to. Placing the observer
at that feature means the subject's attention
and the observer's are on the same object at
the same time, which is the condition the
schedule requires.

The subject is not to be told that the
observer is at the lamp. Subjects have
reported this without being told, in six
runs of nine.

                              M. KETCH
                              rev. 3, 1966"
